From 58dc2397639628f85ed75e28eb3de683feebfa30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] version: add the sphynx version to the release string

Fork-specific, not for upstream. SSH_SPHYNX is the version of the sphynx
packaging, so the release string reads for example
OpenSSH_10.6p1_hpn18.12.0_sphynx0.5.3. It is in the SSH banner, in
"ssh -V", and matched by "Match version". sphynx build refuses to build if
this tag and its own version disagree.

Regenerate this patch when the sphynx version changes.

Changelog: sphynx 0.0.3

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 version.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/version.h b/version.h
index 0e40da38f..ff4e3fe8c 100644
--- a/version.h
+++ b/version.h
@@ -4,4 +4,5 @@
 
 #define SSH_PORTABLE	"p1"
 #define SSH_HPN         "_hpn18.12.0"
-#define SSH_RELEASE	SSH_VERSION SSH_PORTABLE SSH_HPN
+#define SSH_SPHYNX      "_sphynx0.5.3"
+#define SSH_RELEASE	SSH_VERSION SSH_PORTABLE SSH_HPN SSH_SPHYNX
